  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Chronic Crisis - Timor-Leste Country Operational Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Country Operational Plan:Timor-Leste was severely affected by COVID-19 throughout 2021, with cases increasing at the start of the year. The situation was exacerbated by the occurrence of Cyclone Seroja, which drove thousands of people into evacuation centres across the nation, making it difficult to maintain social distancing. By mid-2021, a second wave fuelled by the delta variant had the government fighting to prevent case and death rates from skyrocketing as the health system was under tremendous strain.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In addition, while there may have been economic growth across 2021, a survey on the socio-economic impacts of COVID-19 at the household level, reveals that poor and vulnerable households have been hit much harder by the global pandemic. Although levels of employment in the country improved in 2021, they have not reached pre-pandemic levels and paid work is now more likely to be characterized as informal and insecure. Similarly, while income levels have been somewhat restored, they have not been restored to the same level, and coverage of social protection in the country remains low and does not fully reach poor and vulnerable groups</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Min 7000</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherland Red Cross provided support for CVTL in the area of cash and voucher capacity as part of The Cash and Voucher Assistance Readiness Project to leverage the ability of CVTL to deliver appropriate, accountable and timely cash and voucher assistance. This is aligned with the IFRC&#x2019;s commissioned Cash Roadmap for enhancing cash preparedness in National Societies.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Timor-Leste</narrative>
  </description>
